2. Regulatory Disclosure Obligations
Timely disclosure is a core regulatory obligation. Failure to disclose material information within required timeframes may result in
regulatory sanctions and reputational damage:
 Material Portfolio Changes: Changes representing >5% of NAV must be disclosed to the regulator within 24 hours.
 Quarterly Performance Reports: Audited performance reports must be submitted to the regulatory authority each quarter.
 Major Shareholding Threshold: Equity holdings reaching or exceeding 5% in any listed company trigger public disclosure
obligations.
 Related-Party Transactions: All transactions with affiliated entities must be pre-cleared by the Compliance Officer before
execution.
 Short Position Reporting: Net short positions exceeding 0.2% of issued share capital must be reported under applicable rules.
 Risk Model Changes: Material changes to risk models or key parameters require written regulatory pre-notification.
 ESG Disclosures: Funds marketed as ESG-compliant must publ
